FOLLOWED SOURCE AND DATA
------------------------

src/tqbf/dtoa.rs follows the double-to-text conversion of nlohmann/json
(include/nlohmann/detail/conversions/to_chars.hpp: Grisu2 after Florian
Loitsch, "Printing Floating-Point Numbers Quickly and Accurately with
Integers", PLDI 2010, plus nlohmann's output format), so Torque writes numbers
the way Typesense does.

nlohmann/json  Copyright (c) 2013-2025 Niels Lohmann  MIT License

Torque's segment format and merges follow techniques of Apache Lucene, among
them the SmallFloat norm encoding in src/index/inverted.rs:

Apache Lucene
Copyright 2001-2025 The Apache Software Foundation

This product includes software developed at
The Apache Software Foundation (http://www.apache.org/).

rphonetic (Apache-2.0) is a Rust port of the phonetic encoders of Apache
Commons Codec 1.15; Torque uses its Double Metaphone and its Daitch-Mokotoff
Soundex with the Commons Codec rules (dmrules.txt) compiled in, for
name-matching fields (src/names):

Apache Commons Codec
Copyright 2002-2020 The Apache Software Foundation

This product includes software developed at
The Apache Software Foundation (https://www.apache.org/).

src/names/score.rs follows the logic-v2 name matcher of OpenSanctions' rigour:

rigour  Copyright (c) 2023-2025: OpenSanctions Datenbanken GmbH  MIT License

deunicode (BSD-3-Clause) folds text to ASCII for Torque's tokenizer. Its README
traces its tables to Text::Unidecode, Unicodey, gh emoji and any_ascii:

